**Appendix M – Amendments and Interpretation**

M.1 This Charter may be amended, in whole or in part, by a special resolution of the Committee passed at a duly convened meeting, provided that:

(a) notice of the proposed amendment, setting out the full text of the amendment, has been given to each Member at least fourteen (14) days before the meeting at which the amendment is to be considered; and

(b) the amendment is approved by not less than two-thirds (2/3) of the Members present and voting, whether in person or by electronic means in accordance with clause K.8.

M.2 An amendment to the Charter takes effect on the date specified in the resolution, or, if no date is specified, on the fourteenth (14th) day after the date on which the resolution is passed.

M.3 The Committee may, by ordinary resolution, adopt, amend, or repeal procedural rules, guidelines, and operating manuals that are not inconsistent with this Charter. Such rules, guidelines, and manuals must be recorded in the minutes and made available to all Members.

M.4 If any provision of this Charter is or becomes invalid, illegal, or unenforceable in any jurisdiction, that provision is to be severed from the Charter, and the validity, legality, and enforceability of the remaining provisions is not affected.

M.5 In this Charter, unless the context otherwise requires:

(a) "AOMA" means the Australian Online Marketplace Association, a company limited by guarantee, and "Board" means the board of directors of AOMA;

(b) "Committee" means the MarketGuard Trust & Safety Committee established by this Charter;

(c) "Member" means a person appointed to the Committee in accordance with Appendix A, and includes the Chair and the Deputy Chair;

(d) "Special Resolution" means a resolution passed by a majority of not less than two-thirds (2/3) of the Members present and voting at a meeting of which notice specifying the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution has been duly given;

(e) "Ordinary Resolution" means a resolution passed by a majority of the Members present and voting at a meeting of the Committee;

(f) "Working Day" means a day on which banks are open for general banking business in Sydney, New South Wales, excluding Saturdays, Sundays, and public holidays;

(g) words importing the singular include the plural and vice versa, and words importing a gender include every gender;

(h) a reference to a clause or Appendix is a reference to a clause of or Appendix to this Charter, unless otherwise stated; and

(i) headings are for convenience only and do not affect the interpretation of this Charter.

**Appendix N – Review of the Charter**

N.1 The Committee shall undertake a comprehensive review of this Charter at least once every twenty-four (24) months from the date of its adoption, and may recommend amendments to the Board as a result of that review.

N.2 The review required by clause N.1 shall consider, at a minimum:

(a) the continued appropriateness of the Committee's mandate and functions as set out in Appendix A;

(b) the effectiveness of the Committee's composition and membership arrangements, including the balance of skills and experience among Members;

(c) the adequacy of the Committee's resources, including administrative support and budget;

(d) the operation of the Committee's decision-making and voting procedures under Appendices K and L; and

(e) any changes to applicable laws, regulations, or industry standards affecting online marketplace trust and safety.

N.3 The Committee may at any time, by special resolution, recommend to the Board that a review of this Charter be conducted earlier than required by clause N.1.

**Appendix O – Records and Reporting**

O.1 The Committee shall maintain, or cause to be maintained, the following records:

(a) a register of Members, including the date of each appointment and the date of any resignation or removal;

(b) a register of conflicts of interest declared by Members;

(c) minutes of all meetings of the Committee, including the text of all resolutions passed and the result of any vote taken, recorded in accordance with Appendices K and L;
